# =============================================================================
# How to install these dependencies
# =============================================================================
#
# This is the source file -- edit this, then regenerate the pinned
# requirements.txt with:
#   uv pip compile requirements.in -o requirements.txt
#
# pipx is for standalone CLI tools (one isolated app per install). It does NOT
# replace "pip install -r requirements.txt" for this whole project. Use one of:
#
# --- A) Recommended: project virtualenv (same as pip) ---
#   python3 -m venv .venv
#   .venv/bin/python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
#   .venv/bin/uvicorn src.web.app:app --reload --port 8080
#   .venv/bin/python -m src.main
#
# --- B) pipx: put all libraries into uvicorn’s pipx environment, then run from repo root ---
#   pipx install uvicorn
#   pipx inject uvicorn -r requirements.txt
#   cd /path/to/security-digest
#   uvicorn src.web.app:app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8080
#   python3 -m src.main          # still use system/venv python for the pipeline
#
#   (pipx 1.5+ supports: pipx inject <app> -r requirements.txt)
#
# --- C) pipx + run without global inject (one-off) ---
#   pipx run --spec 'uvicorn[standard]' uvicorn --help   # not ideal for this repo
#
# =============================================================================

